The ${t}_{2g}$ (triplet, lower energy) orbitals are the ${d}_{\mathrm{xy}},{d}_{\mathrm{xz}}$ and ${d}_{\mathrm{yz}}$ orbitals. The ${e}_{g}$ (doublet, higher energy) orbitals are the ${d}_{{z}^{2}}$ and ${d}_{{x}^{2} - {y}^{2}}$ orbitals. These split d-orbitals are called ${t}_{2g}$ and ${e}_{g}$because they are split by the effect of the surrounding ligand ions in a crystal field.

${\left(\mathrm{Cr}{\left({H}_{2}O\right)}_{6}\right)}^{3 + }$ Contains ${\mathrm{Cr}}^{3 + } : \left(\mathrm{Ar}\right)3{d}^{3} : {t}_{2g}^{3}{e}_{g}^{o} {\left(\mathrm{Fe}{\left({H}_{2}O\right)}_{6}\right)}^{3 + }$ Contains ${\mathrm{Fe}}^{3 + } : \left(\mathrm{Ar}\right)3{d}^{5} : {t}_{2g}^{3}{e}_{g}^{2} {\left(\mathrm{Ni}{\left({H}_{2}O\right)}_{6}\right)}^{2 + }$ Contains ${\mathrm{Ni}}^{2 + } : \left(\mathrm{Ar}\right)3{d}^{8} : {t}_{2g}^{6}{e}_{g}^{2} {\left(V{\left({H}_{2}O\right)}_{6}\right)}^{3 + }$ Contains ${V}^{3 + } : \left(\mathrm{Ar}\right)3{d}^{2} : {t}_{2g}^{2}{e}_{g}^{o}$

